  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri. Manivel . R vs Shashikanta Patra on 16 December, 2021 Kabc020317452019 Before Motor Vehicles Accident Claims Tribunal, Bengaluru City Scch4 Present: Raju.M.., M.A., Ll.B., Member, Mact Xviii Addl. Judge, Court of Small Causes, Bengaluru . Dated this the 16th day of December 2021 Mvc No.7606 and 7607/2019 Petitioner/S: Sri.Manivel.R",
    "facts": "on 16 December, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/99699905/ 2 dashed it to the petitioner in MVC No.7606/2019 and SCCH4 4 MVC No.7606 and 7607/2019 pillion rider i.e., petitioner in MVC 7607/2019, consequently both the petitioners sustained injuries. Immediately after the accident, the petitioner in MVC No.7606/2019 was shifted to Sparsh Hospital, Bengaluru where he admitted as an inpatient for one week. This petitioner has sustained injuries such as Left Shaft Tibia Communited Grade II fracture and other multiple injuries and under went surgery of left leg wound debridement, suturing and IM nailing tibia under spinal anesthesia on 16.11.2019 and post operative period was uneventful. The petitioner was very hale and healthy prior to the accident. This petitioner was working as Mechanic and he was earning a sum of Rs.20,000/. Due to the permanent disability sustained in the accident the petitioner is no longer in a position to do his Mechanic work and now is idle without doing any work. SCCH4 5 MVC No.7606 and 7607/2019 Immediately after the accident, the petitioner in MVC No.7607/2019 was also shifted to Sparsh Hospital, Bengaluru. Due to financial constraints the petitioner was shifted to Best Hospital hospital where he was admitted as an inpatient for 15 days. This petitioner has sustained injuries such as Left Intratrochonteric fracture with distal femur fractureSepsis with DIC and other Sri. Manivel . R vs Shashikanta Patra on 16 December, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/99699905/ 3 multiple injuries and under went surgery of left Pen with distal femur plating under anesthesia on 18.11.2019. Post procedure 4 pint PCV transfused, 10 units FFP, 7 pint RDPS transfused. Post operative period was uneventful. This petitioner was working as Mason and he was earning a sum of Rs.20,000/. Due to the permanent disability sustained in the accident the petitioner is no longer in a position to do his mason work and now is idle without doing any work. SCCH4 6 MVC No.7606 and 7607/2019 The respondent No.1 and 2 are the owner and insurer of the offending vehicle. Hence, they are jointly and severally liable to pay the compensation to the petitioners. Hence the petitioners prays to award compensation of Rs.30,00,000/for each ,with interest. 3. After service of notices the respondent No.1 placed exparte. The respondent No.2 has entered appearance through its advocate and filed objection statement. The respondent No.2 has filed statement of objection by admitting the issuance of Package policy to the motor cycle bearing No.OD22L760 and the liability if any is subjected to terms and conditions of the policy. Further contended that, the respondent No.1 has willfully entrusted his vehicle to a person who did not possess the valid and effective driving license to ride the Sri.Manivel.R vs Shashikanta Patra on 16 December, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/99699905/ 4 same as on the date of the accident. The alleged accident SCCH4 7 MVC No.7606 and 7607/2019 was not occurred in the manner as pleaded by the petitioner. The petitioner in MVC.No.7606/19 was main architect for the accident who tried to cross the road where there is no provision for crossing the road by the pedestrians. The petitioner in MVC. No.7607/19 guilty of violation of motor vehicle rules and not wearing the safety helmet, as such he is not entitle for the compensation. The compensation claimed by the petitioners are highly excessive, exorbitant and unreasonable. Accordingly, respondent No.2 prays to dismiss the petition against it. 4. On the basis of rival contention, the following common issues have been framed in all the petitions: 1. In order to prove the claim petitions, the petitioner in MVC No.7606/2019 is examined as PW.1, through him 11 documents are marked at Ex.P1 to11. When the case was put for evidence of respondent, its advocate submitted no evidence on their behalf.",
    "arguments": "18. In the decision reported in 2021 ACJ 1592 in the case Yashodha.H and others V/s Sharath Acharya and another the Hon'ble High Court of Karnataka was please to award the compensation by taking notional income as fixed by the High Court SCCH4 17 MVC No.7606 and 7607/2019 Legal Service committee. In the decision reported in 2021 ACJ 1592 in the case Yashodha.H and others V/s Sharath Acharya and another the Hon'ble High Court of Karnataka was please to award the compensation by taking notional income as fixed by the High Court Legal Service committee. But in the recent judgment, in civil appeal No.6902/2021, in the case of Kurvan Ansari @ Kurvan V/s Shyam Kishore Murmu, the Hon'ble supreme court was pleased to award interest at the rate of 6% p.a.,",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "18. In the decision reported in 2021 ACJ 1592 in the case Yashodha.H and others V/s Sharath Acharya and another the Hon'ble High Court of Karnataka was please to award the compensation by taking notional income as fixed by the High Court SCCH4 17 MVC No.7606 and 7607/2019 Legal Service committee. In the decision reported in 2021 ACJ 1592 in the case Yashodha.H and others V/s Sharath Acharya and another the Hon'ble High Court of Karnataka was please to award the compensation by taking notional income as fixed by the High Court Legal Service committee. But in the recent judgment, in civil appeal No.6902/2021, in the case of Kurvan Ansari @ Kurvan V/s Shyam Kishore Murmu, the Hon'ble supreme court was pleased to award interest at the rate of 6% p.a.,"
  },
